variables = a word that acctually stores a value like some string int 
types
1.var = from ES5 function scoped could be declared twice with the different value
2.let = from ES6 blocked scoped and the value could be changed
3.const = also from the ES6 but the scope is global and value cannot be changed 

temporal dead zone = when we execute the variable before its initialization
hoisting = when a variable is made its declaration goes on top of the code but the initialization remains in its place so that makes the temporal dead zone and it happens in all three types of variables var,let,const but the var shows "UNDEFINED" and let, const gives a refrence error



